WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.625
A sound wave is a pattern of squashed and spread-out particles that travels.

2
00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:10.200
The speaker makes squashed patches and spread-out patches that travel along.

3
00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:16.676
The orange particle only moves to and fro. The wave travels, the particle does not.

4
00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:25.051
More vibrations each second give a higher pitch and shorter waves.

5
00:00:28.487 --> 00:00:31.487
Bigger vibrations make a louder sound.
